// 40_runtime_chain.zp
// Z+ runtime chains: declare a chain whose nodes become real entries in
// the kernel chain registry (chain.h), parented under CHAIN_CPU with
// MASQ_INTERNAL tier. After `run 40_runtime_chain`, the `chains` shell
// command lists `heartbeat_runtime` as a LIVE chain. `inspect <id>`
// shows the three declared nodes (pulse, sustained, tap.log).
//
// chain_registry_tick will resolve the chain every frame via the Z+
// dispatch thunk (zp_kernel_resolve_thunk in zp_runtime.c) which walks
// each node's stored verb AST. B3 stats and MasQ provenance accumulate
// the same way as for any other registered chain.

chain heartbeat_runtime {
  pulse : emit(1) -> sustained(> 0, for = 3) -> tap.log
}
